{"Title":"An Act prohibiting hunting on property owned by the department of correction in the town of Concord.","BillNumber":"S2987","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S29","Name":"Senate Committee on Rules","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S29","ResponseDate":"2024-12-03T12:12:28.827"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2987/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Amendment","Pinslip":"Senate, December 5, 2024 - The committee on Rules to whom was referred House Bill to prohibit hunting on property owned by the Department of Correction and located at 28A Union turnpike in the town of Concord (House, No. 4200); reports, recommending that the same ought to pass with an amendment striking out all after the enacting clause and inserting in place thereof the text of Senate document numbered 2987.","DocumentText":"\tNo person shall discharge a firearm, hunt or in any manner molest or destroy any bird or mammal on the property owned by the department of correction located at 28A Union turnpike in the town of Concord. A violation of this paragraph shall be punishable under section 90 of chapter 131 of the General Laws. The department of correction shall erect and maintain suitable signage at 28A Union turnpike in the town of Concord to provide notice to the public of the prohibition established under this act.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}